# FABLE-SONNET-OWN-LOOKUP-AUDIT-20260923-131 Part 1 probe (measured, NOT
# fixed here -- a "disagrees" row for Part 2). l2_hidden_from's own
# comment says its fallback ("no caller binding: use the declaration in
# the selected callee's lexical node") should resolve a callee's unbound
# dynamic input to THAT callee's own declaration. The fallback actually
# calls l2_own_seg_scan... no -- l2_own_first(nm), which takes no mi/
# callee parameter at all: it scans l2_own_n GLOBALLY for the first
# top-level row (any method) with a matching name. gamma calls beta with
# no binding for `shared` anywhere in the caller chain (entry -> gamma);
# beta reads `shared` as a dynamic input, unbound, before its own binding
# line -- exactly the case the fallback comment describes. alpha, an
# UNRELATED method declared earlier in this file with its own field also
# named `shared` (=111), is what the fallback actually finds and reads,
# because it is simply the first `shared` in source order -- not beta's.
#
# MEASURED on the current tree: prints "beta sees shared=111" (alpha's
# value). This is the same class of cross-method name collision the old
# self-referential `node\x` mechanism had (FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-
# 20260923-121's sticky fixtures' own history) -- l2_own_first ignores mi
# entirely, so ANY earlier-declared method's same-named top-level own
# field wins over the actual callee's. Not asserting a "correct" value
# here: what an unbound dynamic input's fallback should read (beta's own
# not-yet-run declaration? 0? a refusal?) is Part 2's question, an author
# ruling may be needed. This fixture pins today's measured (wrong) value
# so Part 2's fix is mutation-checkable against a known baseline.
fn: alpha () int
    int: shared 111
    return: 0
end: alpha

fn: beta () int
    c.printf: "beta sees shared=%d\n" shared
    int: shared
    shared: 222
    return: 0
end: beta

fn: gamma () int
    beta()
    return: 0
end: gamma

alpha()
gamma()
return: 0
